    "finding": "AuroraPIC produces about 13.1 percent fewer ionizations per starting electron while electron wall loss is only about 3.1 percent lower than native. Its total kinetic energy is about 12.2 percent higher, field energy agrees within 1.6 percent, and its global endpoint energetic fraction is about 6.4 percent lower. The discrepancy is therefore distribution-shaped: lower ionizing-tail replenishment occurs despite greater total kinetic energy, rather than because of excessive wall loss or globally insufficient kinetic energy.",
